# 低频词汇 List09
# 领域: 考研
# 学科: 英语词汇
# 来源: 2024恋练有词
# 描述: 低频词汇List09核心词汇

{{encompass}}{/ɪnˈkʌmpəs/}{包含；涵盖}{The curriculum encompasses a wide range of subjects.}}
{{endorse}}{/ɪnˈdɔːs/}{支持；赞同}{The committee endorsed the proposed changes.}}
{{endure}}{/ɪnˈdjʊər/}{忍受；持久}{The community endured months of hardship after the flood.}}
{{enforce}}{/ɪnˈfɔːs/}{执行；实施}{The police are responsible for enforcing the law.}}
{{engage}}{/ɪnˈɡeɪdʒ/}{从事；吸引}{The speaker engaged the audience with thought-provoking questions.}}
{{enlighten}}{/ɪnˈlaɪtn/}{启发；开导}{The documentary aims to enlighten viewers about environmental issues.}}
{{enrich}}{/ɪnˈrɪtʃ/}{充实；使富裕}{Travel enriches the mind and broadens one's perspective.}}
{{enroll}}{/ɪnˈrəʊl/}{登记；入学}{Over 500 students enrolled in the new program.}}
{{entail}}{/ɪnˈteɪl/}{需要；使承担}{The project entails significant financial investment.}}
{{enthusiastic}}{/ɪnˌθjuːziˈæstɪk/}{热情的；热心的}{The audience gave an enthusiastic response to the performance.}}
{{entitle}}{/ɪnˈtaɪtl/}{给...权利；命名}{Every citizen is entitled to freedom of speech.}}
{{entity}}{/ˈentəti/}{实体；存在}{The organization operates as an independent entity.}}
{{envision}}{/ɪnˈvɪʒn/}{想象；展望}{The architect envisioned a sustainable urban community.}}
{{epidemic}}{/ˌepɪˈdemɪk/}{流行病；蔓延}{The opioid epidemic has affected communities across the nation.}}
{{equivalent}}{/ɪˈkwɪvələnt/}{等价的；相当的}{The qualification is recognized as equivalent to a degree.}}
{{erode}}{/ɪˈrəʊd/}{侵蚀；削弱}{Public trust in institutions has eroded over time.}}
{{escalate}}{/ˈeskəleɪt/}{升级；加剧}{The conflict escalated rapidly in the following weeks.}}
{{espionage}}{/ˈespiənɑːʒ/}{间谍活动；谍报}{The suspect was charged with industrial espionage.}}
{{essence}}{/ˈesns/}{本质；精华}{In essence, the argument boils down to a matter of fairness.}}
{{evacuate}}{/ɪˈvækjueɪt/}{疏散；撤离}{Residents were evacuated before the hurricane made landfall.}}
{{evoke}}{/ɪˈvəʊk/}{引起；唤起}{The painting evokes a sense of nostalgia.}}
{{evolve}}{/ɪˈvɒlv/}{进化；发展}{The strategy evolved over time in response to market changes.}}
{{exaggerate}}{/ɪɡˈzædʒəreɪt/}{夸张；夸大}{The media tends to exaggerate the impact of minor events.}}
{{excerpt}}{/ˈeksɜːpt/}{摘录；节选}{The teacher read an excerpt from the novel to the class.}}
{{exempt}}{/ɪɡˈzempt/}{免除；豁免}{Small businesses are exempt from certain regulations.}}
{{exert}}{/ɪɡˈzɜːt/}{施加；发挥}{The union exerted pressure on management to raise wages.}}
{{exile}}{/ˈeksaɪl/}{流放；流亡}{The political leader spent years in exile.}}
{{exotic}}{/ɪɡˈzɒtɪk/}{异国的；奇异的}{The garden features exotic plants from tropical regions.}}
{{explicit}}{/ɪkˈsplɪsɪt/}{明确的；直言的}{The guidelines provide explicit instructions for the process.}}
{{extract}}{/ɪkˈstrækt/}{提取；摘录}{The machine extracts juice from fresh fruit.}}
